course: dictionary
lesson: 3081
title: Reading a dinosaur word in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A name like Edmontosaurus looks hard, but the words around it give you clues. Look at the other words in the sentence first. Here the sentence says «Duck-billed dinosaurs, or hadrosaurs, such as Edmontosaurus», so you can see Edmontosaurus is one kind of duck-billed dinosaur.
explain: The word «or» is a clue too. It means two words are the same thing, so hadrosaurs is another name for duck-billed dinosaurs. The words «such as» mean "for example", so Edmontosaurus is one example of that group.
explain: The sentence also tells you what this dinosaur ate. «Hundreds of teeth packed together to grind plants» tells you it was a plant-eater. To check, put your meaning in place of the hard word: "Duck-billed dinosaurs, or plant-eating dinosaurs, such as plant-eaters..." makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: Edmontosaurus was a large plant-eating duck-billed dinosaur, also called a hadrosaur.
fact: It lived in North America near the end of the age of dinosaurs, about 68 to 66 million years ago.
fact: Its name comes from Edmonton in Alberta, Canada, where the first fossils were found.
fact: «Edmontosaurus» is the name of its group, so a scientist can write it the same way for all of them.
fact: Some Edmontosaurus fossils even show skin, which tells scientists more about how it looked.
exercise: «Duck-billed dinosaurs, or hadrosaurs, such as Edmontosaurus had hundreds of teeth packed together to grind plants.» What does hadrosaurs mean in this sentence? | *Another name for duck-billed dinosaurs | A type of rock | A place in Canada | A kind of meat-eating dinosaur
exercise: Edmontosaurus is named after a place. Which country is that place in? | Australia | *Canada | Egypt | Mexico
exercise: Which word means a large group of animals living together? | skin | *herd | fossil | hadrosaur
test: «Duck-billed dinosaurs, or hadrosaurs, such as Edmontosaurus had hundreds of teeth packed together to grind plants.» Which word in this sentence tells you what the teeth were used for? | hundreds | *grind | duck-billed | packed
test: Mia reads that Edmontosaurus was hunted by Tyrannosaurus rex. What does hunted most likely mean here? | Looked after kindly | Found under the ground | *Chased and caught for food | Drawn in a book
exam: Using the clues in «Duck-billed dinosaurs, or hadrosaurs, such as Edmontosaurus had hundreds of teeth packed together to grind plants.», what kind of food did Edmontosaurus eat? | Insects | *Plants | Meat | Fish
